## 5. Non-redundant gene catalogue (Prodigal + CD-HIT-EST) and quantification (Salmon)

**Gene prediction — Prodigal v2.6.3**, in metagenomic mode (`-p meta`), on the filtered contigs. Only **complete** open reading frames (ORFs) (not truncated at either end) with a length ≥300 bp are retained, to avoid including partial gene fragments that could bias downstream functional analyses.

**Non-redundant catalogue — CD-HIT-EST:** clusters near-identical genes (95% nucleotide identity, 90% coverage of the shorter sequence) and keeps one representative sequence per cluster. This reduces redundancy arising from genes shared across samples or overlapping assembly fragments.

**Quantification — Salmon v1.10.3**, in metagenomic mode (`--meta`): an index is built from the non-redundant catalogue, and gene abundance (in TPM and raw read counts) is quantified separately for each of the seven samples, producing a sample × gene abundance matrix.

---

## 6. Functional annotation of the gene catalogue

Three complementary databases are used to annotate genes in the non-redundant catalogue:

| Database | Tool | Version | What it provides |
|---|---|---|---|
| eggNOG v5.0.2 | eggNOG-mapper | v2.1.7 | Functional orthology: COG, KEGG (KO), CAZy |
| CAZyDB | dbCAN2 (via DIAMOND blastp) | — | Cross-check of carbohydrate-active enzymes (CAZy) |
| CARD | RGI | v6.0.5 | Antimicrobial resistance genes |

**eggNOG-mapper** is run on the translated proteins of the non-redundant catalogue using DIAMOND as the search engine; the resulting KEGG/COG/CAZy annotations are combined with the Salmon abundance matrix (TPM) to obtain quantitative functional profiles per sample.

**dbCAN2** is used as an independent check of eggNOG's CAZy annotations, via direct DIAMOND search against CAZyDB.

**RGI/CARD** identifies antimicrobial resistance genes in the protein catalogue, reporting both strict and "loose" (more permissive) hits, useful for resistome surveillance in an environmental/aquaculture monitoring context.

